"""Derive SkyyWardrobe/build_skyywardrobe_0.2.13.py from the SET pin 0.2.12 (build_skyywardrobe_0.2.12.py, GENERATED by
tools/wardrobe_0_2_12_patch.py; 0.2.12 stays untouched) AND SkyyWardrobe/test_skyywardrobe_0.2.13.py from test_skyywardrobe_0.2.12.py.
Edit THIS file, never the generated scripts: python tools/wardrobe_0_2_13_patch.py, then python SkyyWardrobe/build_skyywardrobe_0.2.13.py
(never --deploy from an agent). Test: python SkyyWardrobe/test_skyywardrobe_0.2.13.py
Every anchor is asserted once; at the end every change is undone on a copy and compared with the source (nothing else changed).

0.2.13 (2026-10-30, rarity pass) - PROJECT-RULES 4 rarity colours everywhere; pet rows + cells. LOOKS ONLY: no saved-data change, no
setting, no lang key, no command, no behaviour change; rollback to 0.2.12 is safe (no data, no floor).
Skyy (2026-10-24): "make that the global default. if it has a rarity, it gets color coded." + (2026-10-18) "color code everything. so
you can see what stats it gives at a glance". The colours = SkyyPets 0.4.18 / 0.4.20's RARITY_COLORS (vanilla item Quality colours
Common .. Legendary + the SkyyGear Mythic colour), in the same order.
  1. WdBridge.petRar(label) = the rarity word of a pets:fn:petName label ("Rare Wolf Lv 12" -> "Rare"; the rarRank word list; "" = none)
     and WdBridge.rarCol(word) = its colour (a generated if-chain like WdPage.rcol; anything else = the default text colour).
  2. WdPage.petIcon: after the kind portrait Skyy_PetIcon_<Kind> is found (SkyyPets' file kind, else the label guess), the HIDDEN rarity
     portrait Skyy_PetIcon_<Kind>_<Rarity> (SkyyPets 0.4.18+: the same picture + the rarity's Quality) is used when the client knows it
     (safe()) - the item carries the rarity Quality for any client view that reads it. NOTE: Requip draws icons as a plain ItemIcon,
     which draws NO Quality frame and has no hover popup, so the visible rarity frame is the square of 4 / 5 below. An older SkyyPets /
     a kind without that item / a label without a rarity word = the plain portrait (unchanged, no client warning). All three callers get
     it: the picker rows, the loadout Pet / Summon cells, the live pet in a Keep cell.
  3. WdPage.refList: each pet row's name is drawn in its rarity colour (the row's colour element -> the existing 'rc' label colour);
     Keep / None rows and the modifier / ability rows (no rarity in their data) stay the default colour.
  4. (review fix) the picker's pet rows get the rarity SQUARE behind the icon (kit icon_cell icon_bg = SkyyPets 0.4.18 / SkyyBazaar 0.2.3:
     the rarity colour at 40 %, a 2 px frame + tint; no rarity word = the faint grey) through their own row templates RZ<k>P<S|D|N>,
     picked by a 9th row element (WdBridge.rarBg); gear / item / Pocket / ability / modifier rows keep the 0.2.12 templates byte for byte.
  5. (review fix) the loadout Pet / Summon cells: the same square behind the icon + the NAME in the rarity colour (refViews' pet entries
     gain [5] name colour + [6] square colour); Keep (empty) / None / Gone pet = the default colour; ability / modifier cells unchanged.
Not changed: the sectioned pet tooltip (it stays on the Pets page), gear rows (no square: outside this round), the cell / row text.
Classes: WdBridge + petRar / rarCol / rarBg; bodies: WdPage.petIcon, WdPage.refList, WdPage.refViews, the page build.
"""
import os
import re

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
HERE = os.path.join(ROOT, "SkyyWardrobe")
LF = "\n"


class Patch(object):
    def __init__(self, src, dst, tag):
        raw = open(src, "rb").read()
        self.nl = "\r\n" if b"\r\n" in raw else "\n"
        assert self.nl == "\n" or raw.count(b"\r\n") == raw.count(b"\n"), "mixed line endings in " + src
        self.s = raw.decode("utf8").replace("\r\n", "\n")
        self.old = self.s
        self.src, self.dst, self.tag = src, dst, tag
        self.changes = []

    def has(self, t):
        return t in self.s

    def rep(self, old, new):
        n = self.s.count(old)
        assert n == 1, "%s anchor count %d: %s" % (self.tag, n, old[:140])
        assert self.s.count(new) == 0, "%s: the new text already exists: %s" % (self.tag, new[:100])
        self.s = self.s.replace(old, new, 1)
        self.changes.append((new, old))

    def finish(self):
        u = self.s
        for new, old in reversed(self.changes):
            assert u.count(new) == 1, "%s: a change is not unique any more: %s" % (self.tag, new[:100])
            u = u.replace(new, old, 1)
        assert u == self.old, "%s: the generated script differs from the source outside the recorded changes" % self.tag
        compile(self.s, self.dst, "exec")
        open(self.dst, "w", encoding="utf8", newline="").write(self.s.replace(LF, self.nl) if self.nl != LF else self.s)
        print("wrote", os.path.relpath(self.dst, ROOT), "(%d lines; source %d; %d changes, undo-compare OK)" % (self.s.count(LF), self.old.count(LF), len(self.changes)))


